      "decision_id": "dec-isp-003",
      "question": "Approve the enforceable legacy Sub transition rule, including its narrow exception workflow for bounded in-place module adoption that retires one local writer?",
      "owner": "Michael Ayoade",
      "resolution": "Approved. The legacy Sub transition rule is: no new cohort writer and no growth of an existing one; bounded in-place module adoption is admitted only when it retires a local writer. Enforcement is the two-directional cohort writer ratchets in dotmac_sub, which fail the build on an added or grown writer and on a removed writer whose baseline was not lowered in the same change.",
